(in-ns 'go.arbace.wai) (go/file "w2g.go" :imports [

    ;; w2g (doc/wasm/WAI.md §9; doc/wasm/WASM-SURVEY.md §7, WAS10 (a), WA7): a module's functions translated to Go, compiled by Go
    ;; with wai into an AOT program in which each translated function runs as Go code in place of the interpreter. The unit is wai's
    ;; internal code (§3): its static stack heights make every operand a slot of the frame known at translation, its branches carry
    ;; their targets, so a function becomes one Go function with a label a branch target and a goto a branch; each instruction that
    ;; is not a transfer of control is the interpreter's own case (w2gCases, generated from exec.go by `waidriver w2g-cases`) with
    ;; the instruction's fields made constants. The calling convention is the interpreter's (the arguments and results on the
    ;; machine's stack at the frame's base), so translated and interpreted functions call each other and the hosts freely. A
    ;; function with try_table's handlers or a tail call is left to the interpreter (the first part of WA7). The translated
    ;; functions are registered by the module's SHA-256 (RegisterAOT) and attached at instantiation.


